ker D, et al. Understanding primary care physicians&#x02019; propensity to assess elderly patients for depression using interaction and survey data. Med Care. 2005;43(12):1217-24. <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16299433</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR10"><label>10.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Feinstien</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Cicchetti</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>High agreement but low kappa: I. The problems of two paradoxes</article-title><source>J Clin Epidemiol</source><year>1990</year><volume>43</volume><issue>6</issue><fpage>543</fpage><lpage>549</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/0895-4356(90)90158-L</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Feinstien A, Cicchetti D. High agreement but low kappa: I. The problems of two paradoxes. J Clin Epidemiol. 1990;43(6):543&#x02013;9. <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">2348207</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR11"><label>11.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Cicchetti</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Feinstein</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>High agreement but low kappa: II. Resolving the paradoxes</article-title><source>J Clin Epidemiol</source><year>1990</year><volume>43</volume><issue>6</issue><fpage>551</fpage><lpage>558</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/0895-4356(90)90159-M</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Cicchetti D, Feinstein A. High agreement but low kappa: II. Resolving the paradoxes. J Clin Epidemiol. 1990;43(6):551&#x02013;8. <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">2189948</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR12"><label>12.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Bakeman</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Quera</surname><given-names>V</given-names></name><name><surname>McArther</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Robinson</surname><given-names>BF</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Detecting sequential patterns and determining their reliability with fallible observers</article-title><source>Psychol Methods</source><year>1997</year><volume>2</volume><issue>4</issue><fpage>357</fpage><lpage>370</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1037/1082-989X.2.4.357</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Bakeman R, Quera V, McArther D, Robinson BF. Detecting sequential patterns and determining their reliability with fallible observers. Psychol Methods. 1997;2(4):357&#x02013;70. </citation></ref><ref id="CR13"><label>13.</label><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Ickes</surname><given-names>W</given-names></name><name><surname>Marangoni</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Garcia</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name></person-group><person-group person-group-type="editor"><name><surname>Ickes</surname><given-names>W</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Studying empathic accuracy in a clinically relevant context</article-title><source>Empathic Accuracy</source><year>1997</year><publisher-loc>New York</publisher-loc><publisher-name>Guilford Press</publisher-name><fpage>282</fpage><lpage>310</lpage></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Ickes W, Marangoni C, Garcia S. Studying empathic accuracy in a clinically relevant context. In: Ickes W, ed. Empathic Accuracy. New York: Guilford Press; 1997:282&#x02013;310. </citation></ref><ref id="CR14"><label>14.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Eide</surname><given-names>HQV</given-names></name><name><surname>Graugaard</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Finset</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Physician&#x02013;patient dialogue surrounding patients&#x02019; expression of concern: applying sequence analysis to RIAS</article-title><source>Soc Sci Med</source><year>2004</year><volume>59</volume><issue>1</issue><fpage>145</fpage><lpage>155</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/j.socscimed.2003.10.011</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Eide HQV, Graugaard P, Finset A. Physician&#x02013;patient dialogue surrounding patients&#x02019; expression of concern: applying sequence analysis to RIAS. Soc Sci Med. 2004;59(1):145&#x02013;55. <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15087150</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR15"><label>15.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Ware</surname><given-names>JE</given-names></name><name><surname>Kosinski</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Bayliss</surname><given-names>MS</given-names></name><name><surname>McHorney</surname><given-names>CA</given-names></name><name><surname>Rogers</surname><given-names>WH</given-names></name><name><surname>Raczek</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Comparison of methods for the scoring and statistical analysis of SF-36 health profile and summary measures: summary of results from the medical outcomes study</article-title><source>Med Care</source><year>1995</year><volume>33</volume><issue>4 Suppl</issue><fpage>AS264</fpage><lpage>AS279</lpage></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Ware JE Jr., Kosinski M, Bayliss MS, McHorney CA, Rogers WH, Raczek A. Comparison of methods for the scoring and statistical analysis of SF-36 health profile and summary measures: summary of results from the medical outcomes study. Med Care. 1995;33(4 Suppl):AS264&#x02013;79. <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7723455</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR16"><label>16.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Balsa</surname><given-names>AI</given-names></name><name><surname>McGuire</surname><given-names>TG</given-names></name><name><surname>Meredith</surname><given-names>LS</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Testing for statistical discrimination in health care</article-title><source>Health Serv Res</source><year>2005</year><volume>40</volume><issue>1</issue><fpage>227</fpage><lpage>252</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1111/j.1475-6773.2005.00351.x</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Balsa AI, McGuire TG, Meredith LS. Testing for statistical discrimination in health care. Health Serv Res. 2005;40(1):227&#x02013;52. <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15663711</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR17"><label>17.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Bertakis</surname><given-names>KD</given-names></name><name><surname>Callahan</surname><given-names>EJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Helms</surname><given-names>LJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Azari</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Robbins</surname><given-names>JA</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The effect of patient health status on physician practice style</article-title><source>Fam Med</source><year>1993</year><volume>25</volume><issue>8</issue><fpage>530</fpage><lpage>535</lpage></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Bertakis KD, Callahan EJ, Helms LJ, Azari R, Robbins JA. The effect of patient health status on physician practice style. Fam Med. 1993;25(8):530&#x02013;5. <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8405802</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR18"><label>18.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Sleath</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Rubin</surname><given-names>RH</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Gender, ethnicity, and